# OpenClaw — Skill Contract

## The Skill Interface

Every skill in the registry MUST conform to this interface (defined in `lib/skill-contract/src/index.ts`):

```typescript
export type SkillCategory =
  | "RESEARCH"
  | "GENERATE"
  | "VALIDATE"
  | "SEND"
  | "ANALYZE"
  | "TRANSFORM"
  | "ENRICH";

export interface SkillOutput {
  success: boolean;
  data: Record<string, unknown>;
  metadata?: {
    tokensUsed?: number;
    connectorsCalled?: string[];
    graphsQueried?: string[];
    executionMs?: number;
  };
  error?: string;
}

export interface SkillContext {
  tenantId: number;
  userId: string;
  connectors: Record<string, string>;  // connector slug → decrypted credential
  graphIds: number[];
  runId: string;
}

export interface Skill<TInput = Record<string, unknown>> {
  id: string;                    // "ir-research-v1" — kebab-case
  name: string;                  // "Investor Research"
  version: string;               // "1.0.0"
  category: SkillCategory;
  description: string;
  inputs: object;                // JSON Schema
  outputs: object;               // JSON Schema
  requiredConnectors: string[];  // ["crunchbase", "linkedin"]
  requiredGraphs: string[];      // ["investor-profiles"]
  execute: (input: TInput, ctx: SkillContext) => Promise<SkillOutput>;
}

export interface ConnectorDef {
  slug: string;
  name: string;
  authType: "api_key" | "oauth2";
  credentialLabel: string;
  verify?: (credential: string) => Promise<boolean>;
}
```

## Skill Installation Flow

When a tenant installs a skill:
1. Platform checks if required connectors are authorized (prompts OAuth/API key if not)
2. Platform checks if required graphs exist (prompts to create if not)
3. Benchmark gate runs (`quick` test suite via `BENCHMARK_SERVICE_URL`)
4. If benchmark passes (CERTIFIED or CONDITIONAL), skill appears in agent's tool palette
5. Agent can call it from any playbook

## Archon-Generated Skills

Skills can be auto-generated via the Zeta Skill Forge pipeline:

```
POST /archon/generate
{ "description": "Build a skill that fetches RSS headlines for a company" }
```

Pipeline: `prompt → generate (Qwen3 Coder 480B) → L0 validate (tsc) → fix loop (max 2) → L1-L4 benchmark → catalog`

Generated skills must:
- Export `name`, `description`, `inputSchema`, `outputSchema`, `run()` as named exports
- Be under 300 lines
- Use only Node.js built-ins + global `fetch` (no external npm imports)
- Handle all errors in `run()` — never throw, return `{ error: string }` on failure

## Benchmark Grades

| Grade | Meaning | Install allowed? |
|---|---|---|
| CERTIFIED | Passes all L1-L4 levels | Yes |
| CONDITIONAL | Passes with caveats | Yes (with warning) |
| FAILED | Below threshold | No — blocked |
| INCONCLUSIVE | Benchmark service offline | Yes (with warning) |

## Skill Categories (Archon-generated)

Archon uses these categories for generated skills:
- Data, Finance, Productivity, HR & Payroll, Operations, Legal & Compliance, Research, Communication

## Vertical Skill Bundles

A vertical is just a bundle of skills + graphs + connectors + playbooks:

```
IR Skill Bundle v1.0
├── ir-research.skill.ts      → finds investors
├── ir-outreach.skill.ts      → drafts emails
├── ir-pitch.skill.ts         → answers diligence
├── graphs/
│   ├── investor-profiles.graph
│   └── data-room.graph
├── connectors/
│   ├── crunchbase.connector
│   └── gmail.connector
└── playbooks/
    └── full-ir-workflow.playbook
```

Any tenant installs this bundle in one click. Their data, their connectors, same infrastructure.

## Skill Registry (DB)

Skills are stored in the `skills` table. 791+ real skills loaded from GitHub `awesome-openclaw-skills`. 30 categories. 24hr in-process TTL cache. Manual refresh via `POST /api/skills/refresh`.

Tenant-installed skills are tracked in `tenant_skills` (many-to-many).
